 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+### 2Q Eviction Policy
+
+Use 2Q eviction to protect reused comparison sheets from one-off sequential screening scans. 2Q maintains two queues:
+
+- **A1 (FIFO, first-use)**: newly rendered sheets enter here. Size: 3 GiB (25% of the 12 GiB budget).
+- **Am (LRU, reused)**: sheets accessed a second time while in A1 are promoted to Am. Size: 9 GiB (75% of budget).
+
+**Admission**: a newly rendered sheet enters A1. If A1 is full, evict A1's oldest entry before admission.
+
+**Hit while in A1**: the sheet is removed from A1 and promoted to Am. If Am is full, evict Am's LRU entry before promotion.
+
+**Hit while in Am**: move the sheet to Am's MRU position.
+
+**Miss (not in A1 or Am)**: render and admit to A1 as above.
+
+The 25/75 split is the starting configuration. If screening patterns shift heavily toward long sequential scans with few repeated comparisons, or vice versa, the split can be adjusted. The split parameter and all queue state remain private to the preview worker.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q (dual-queue with A1 FIFO + Am LRU) | LRU (single queue), frequency-based eviction with aging | Protects reused comparison sheets from eviction during long sequential screenings. LRU would evict recently used comparison sheets during a scan. Frequency-based aging adds counter maintenance and can lag when editors switch projects. 2Q resists scans at the cost of two queues and a size-split parameter to tune. |
+| Queue size split | 25% A1 (first-use), 75% Am (reused) | 50/50 split, 10/90 split | Sized for the observed workload: editors alternate long screenings (many one-use sheets) with repeated comparisons (small reused set). 25% A1 holds a reasonable sequential window without starving Am. Adjustable if patterns shift. |
+
